#X obj 668 8 seq.nbangs;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 356 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Outputs a given number of bangs at a fixed or variable
time interval. The number of bangs is set by the argument N or the
@n property \, and the interval between bangs by @t. Unlike [seq.bangs]
\, which cycles through a pattern of durations \, this object simply
produces N evenly-spaced bangs.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Repeating a trigger N times — sending a fixed number
of events \, for example a short drum roll \, a burst of notes \, or
a temporary stutter of a sound \, and then stopping automatically.;
#X text 250 279 • Accelerando or ritardando — using @accel and @curve
to make the interval between bangs gradually decrease or increase \,
so that the same number of events is compressed or stretched over time.;
#X text 250 349 • Counted event bursts — firing a fixed number of control
messages for a specific process (for example \, N steps of an arpeggio
or N pulses of a modulation envelope) \, without needing a separate
counter object.;
